Redis structure: {
classes: a copy of the "classes" collection from mongo
lastUpdatedClasses: a time (in milliseconds) equal to when the redis cache was last updated
}
new collection called "lastUpdated" which only has 1 document in it, currently only stores a Date value for "classes". This is the last time that the classes collection (in MONGO specifically, NOT redis) has been updated.
This means when we add 2000 classes, redis wont update 2000 times. Redis will only update when the GET /classes/ route is called

